# Local backups / IDE session state - not source
*.zip
GameForgerEditorLayout.ini
vc140.pdb

# Scratch asset dump at the repo root (~610 MB of .glb). NOT the editor's asset
# root - every code path reads Game/Models (see Editor/src/main.cpp's
# modelsDirectory), and nothing references this directory. Ignored so a routine
# `git add -A` can't commit it into a history that already carries 331 MB of
# binary assets with no LFS.
/models/

# Performance panel exports (Reports/performance-<timestamp>.md). Diagnostic
# output about a particular run on a particular machine - useful to share by
# hand, not to version.
/Reports/

# Game assets are NOT versioned. Models and textures are the actual weight -
# 376 MB and 46 MB respectively - and they cannot be diffed or merged. Demo
# content is published as a download from the website instead.
Game/Models/
Game/Textures/
Game/Cutscenes/
Game/Saves/

# Audio and animation binaries, but keep the .keep placeholders so the folders
# survive a fresh clone - the editor and Project.json expect them to exist.
Game/Audio/*
!Game/Audio/.keep
Game/Animations/*
!Game/Animations/.keep

# Deliberately still tracked, despite sitting under Game/:
#   Game/Scenes/*.gfprod|.gfai  - text JSON, ~760 KB for all four, and
#     Project.json's startupScene points at Castle.gfai. Ignoring these would
#     save 0.2% of the repo and leave a fresh clone unable to open a project.
#   Game/Characters/*.skeleton.json - 1 KB, referenced by Project.json.
#   Game/Branding/logo.jpg + engine.png - editor splash and Runtime boot
#     image; without them a fresh clone launches with a missing splash.
